  "description": "disk fail without --yes says what it would do and exits with 3. With --yes the disk is failed: never read again, its copies count for nothing and are no source, so the next pass makes the replica elsewhere at once, from the other copy, and its mergerfs branch is read-only, after the others. A failed disk cannot be drained, and is taken out even though files still have copies there.",
